{"id":"belshazzar","name":"Belshazzar","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:belshazzar"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Belshazzar","text":"Bel protect the king!, the last of the kings of Babylon (Dan. 5:1). He was the son of Nabonidus by Nitocris, who was the daughter of Nebuchadnezzar and the widow of Nergal-sharezer. When still young he made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and when heated with wine sent for the sacred vessels his “father” (Dan. 5:2), or grandfather, Nebuchadnezzar had carried away from the temple in Jerusalem, and he and his princes drank out of them. In the midst of their mad revelry a hand was seen by the king tracing on the wall the announcement of God’s judgment, which that night fell upon him. At the instance of the queen (i.e., his mother) Daniel was brought in, and he interpreted the writing. That night the kingdom of the Chaldeans came to an end, and the king was slain (Dan. 5:30). (See NERGAL-SHAREZER.) The absence of the name of Belshazzar on the monuments was long regarded as an …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4430","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":15,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4437","lemma":"מַלְכוּ","xlit":"malkûw","gloss":"dominion","kjv":"kingdom, kingly, realm, reign","count":9,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H3792","lemma":"כְּתָב","xlit":"kᵉthâb","gloss":"{something written","kjv":"prescribing, writing","count":7,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H116","lemma":"אֱדַיִן","xlit":"ʼĕdayin","gloss":"then","kjv":"now, that time, then","count":8,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H1722","lemma":"דְּהַב","xlit":"dᵉhab","gloss":"gold","kjv":"gold","count":7,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H1113","lemma":"בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר","xlit":"Bêlshaʼtstsar","gloss":"{Belshatstsar, a Babylonian king}","kjv":"Belshazzar","count":6,"share":0.2}],"verses":["Dan.5.1","Dan.5.2","Dan.5.3","Dan.5.5","Dan.5.6","Dan.5.7","Dan.5.8","Dan.5.9","Dan.5.10","Dan.5.11","Dan.5.12","Dan.5.13","Dan.5.17","Dan.5.18","Dan